I made no source changes this run. The prior reports name no defect in the controls and audio files, so there was nothing to repair. The report is `artifacts/logs/coder_input_audio.SEwuBm/report.md`, and it starts with `FINDINGS`.

- **Pause and music:** The last report said music keeps playing during Pause. I checked that with a headless probe in a real game. Pause stops note scheduling and silences the voices, and unpausing resumes them, which matches vanilla Doom. The Esc menu doesn't pause music, which is also vanilla. The probe and its output are in the same folder as the report.
- **Source state:** The source hash and `dist/doom.wasm` hash are unchanged from the other current reports, so the earlier tester and reviewer evidence still applies.
- **Not verified:** Nobody has listened to the sound effects or music, and nobody has tested a real hidden tab. Those need a human, following the protocol in `tests/README.md`. The probe only shows what the audio code schedules, not how it sounds.
- **Your decisions:** WASD and mouse controls, OPL-faithful music (it is currently an oscillator synth), and saving volume settings across reloads. I added none of these because no requirement was supplied. Any of them changes the wasm, so the coder would need to rebuild and the tester rerun `tests/verify.sh`.